  "fullName": "mkRat",
  "endPos": 805,
  "detail":
  "```lean\nmkRat (num : ℤ) (den : ℕ) : ℚ\n```\n***\nConstruct a rational number from a numerator and denominator.\nThis is a \"smart constructor\" that divides the numerator and denominator by\nthe gcd to ensure that the resulting rational number is normalized, and returns\nzero if `den` is zero.\n\n***\n*import Batteries.Data.Rat.Basic*",
  "definitionStartPos": {"line": 83, "column": 4},
  "definitionPath":
  "/Users/hattoriseiji/Autoinformalization/ExportInfos/./.lake/packages/batteries//Batteries/Data/Rat/Basic.lean",
  "definitionEndPos": {"line": 83, "column": 9}},
 {"startPos": 807,
  "moduleName": "Mathlib.Data.Int.Sqrt",
  "kind": "definition",
  "fullName": "Int.sqrt",
  "endPos": 815,
  "detail":
  "```lean\nInt.sqrt (z : ℤ) : ℤ\n```\n***\n`sqrt z` is the square root of an integer `z`. If `z` is positive, it returns the largest\ninteger `r` such that `r * r ≤ n`. If it is negative, it returns `0`. For example, `sqrt (-1) = 0`,\n`sqrt 1 = 1`, `sqrt 2 = 1` \n***\n*import Mathlib.Data.Int.Sqrt*",
  "definitionStartPos": {"line": 26, "column": 4},
  "definitionPath":
  "/Users/hattoriseiji/Autoinformalization/ExportInfos/./.lake/packages/mathlib//Mathlib/Data/Int/Sqrt.lean",
  "definitionEndPos": {"line": 26, "column": 8}},
